  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nWe look to remain generally dry with continued above-normal warmth \non Sunday and Monday as the upper ridge amplifies. Daily highs look \nto continue running in the mid-90s to low-100s, with potential for \neven warmer heat indices.\n\nThe next curveball in the forecast arrives on Tuesday into \nWednesday, as a strong upper trough begins to round the periphery of \nthe ridge. There is increasingly strong agreement that this feature \nwill push a notable front southward across the Plains during this \ntime. If this occurs, and reaches our area, \"less hot\" conditions\nwould materialize towards the end of the period. As of this \nmorning, grand ensemble guidance shows a medium (30-60%) chance\nfor daytime highs <90 deg F across portions of western into \nnorthern Oklahoma from Tuesday onward.\n\nUngar",
